$2$. $\frac{2}{9} \times 100$, then $500\text{ ml}$.
Answer: Millet about $22.22$% (water about $77.78$%); in $500\text{ ml}$ about $111.1\text{ ml}$ (exactly $500 \times \frac{2}{9}$, about $111.11\text{ ml}$)

$1$. $20$% takes $18$ days;
$2$. $100$% is five times that.
Answer: $90$ days. The assumption is needed because the calculation only works if the same share is picked each day (same workers, same speed).

